# No environment variables, Redis, database or writable disk are required for
# standard calls on Vercel. Use the Next.js preset and Node.js 22.x.
# Never place secrets in NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables.

# Optional: improve connectivity behind restrictive NAT/firewalls or hide the
# participants' IP addresses from each other. Requires your own coturn service.
# Only temporary relay credentials are returned; the shared secret stays here.
# TURN_URLS=turns:turn.example.com:5349?transport=tcp
# TURN_SHARED_SECRET=
# WEBRTC_RELAY_ONLY=true
# Relay-only refuses calls if TURN is missing/misconfigured, with no direct fallback.
# If enabling TURN, apply Vercel Firewall limits to POST /api/call-config
# and coturn user/total allocation quotas: the app is public and has no accounts.

# Optional for non-Vercel hosting ONLY: an IP header overwritten by your trusted
# reverse proxy. On Vercel the platform's x-vercel-forwarded-for is used instead.
# TRUSTED_IP_HEADER=x-real-ip
